@startuml agent_step_sequence
title One agent step — observe → propose → gate → act → verify
autonumber
actor Human as U
participant "Agent loop (code)" as L
participant "Muse Spark 1.3" as M
participant "Safety gate (code)" as G
participant "Browser (Playwright)" as B
participant "Verifier (code)" as V

L -> B : observe()
B --> L : compact element list\n(no raw DOM, no screenshot)
L -> M : goal + elements + tool schemas
M --> L : ONE tool call\n(navigate | click | type | select | finish)
L -> G : classify(action)
alt off allowlist or malformed
  G --> L : DENY (logged, not executed)
else irreversible class
  G -> U : AWAITING_APPROVAL
  U --> G : approve / take over / abort
else safe class
  G --> L : ALLOW
end
L -> B : act(action)
B --> L : result + screenshot
L -> V : success checks
V --> L : pass / fail (never asks the model)
note over M, G
  The model can only escalate (ask for approval).
  It can never widen the allowlist or downgrade a risk class.
end note
@enduml
